HOW TO CREATE .nojekyll IN GITHUB (if download fails):

OPTION 1 - In GitHub website:
1. Go to your repo: CINEMORA-AI
2. Click "Add file" -> "Create new file"
3. Name it: .nojekyll
4. Leave content EMPTY
5. Click "Commit new file"

OPTION 2 - On your computer:
1. Open Notepad
2. Save empty file as ".nojekyll" (with dot)
3. Upload to GitHub

This file is EMPTY (0 bytes) - that's normal!
It tells GitHub Pages: Don't try to build with Jekyll, just serve HTML.
This fixes RED X deployment failure!
